Relevant columns and their potential usage
• `date`: filter and extract calendar years (2022 vs 2023).  
• `item_number`: stable key that identifies an individual liquor product.  
• `item_description`: human‑readable label to display the product.  
• `sale_dollars`: numeric field that holds the revenue that the store paid; used to sum yearly sales.  

Typical conditions you may need
• `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)` or `FORMAT_DATE('%Y', date)` to isolate a year.  
• `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)` to keep only the two comparison years.  
• `sale_dollars IS NOT NULL` to avoid NULL arithmetic (optional).  
• Exclude rows where 2022 sales are zero (to avoid divide‑by‑zero) when computing % growth.  

Below are ten BigQuery SQL snippets that progress from simple exploration to the final query required by the task.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at raw rows to get a feel for the dataset.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List distinct calendar years that appear in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) AS sales_year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
ORDER BY sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show a sample of distinct item numbers and their descriptions.
SELECT DISTINCT item_number, item_description
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE item_number IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Aggregate total sales dollars by calendar year (all items).
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) AS sales_year,
  SUM(sale_dollars)            AS total_sales_dollars
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
GROUP BY sales_year
ORDER BY sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Aggregate 2023 revenue for each item (top 20 by dollars).
SELECT
  item_number,
  item_description,
  SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2023
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2023
GROUP BY item_number, item_description
ORDER BY sales_2023 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Aggregate 2022 revenue for each item (top 20 by dollars).
SELECT
  item_number,
  item_description,
  SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2022
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2022
GROUP BY item_number, item_description
ORDER BY sales_2022 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Join yearly aggregations to put 2022 and 2023 side‑by‑side per item.
WITH y22 AS (
  SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2022
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2022
  GROUP BY item_number
),
y23 AS (
  SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2023
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2023
  GROUP BY item_number
)
SELECT
  y23.item_number,
  COALESCE(y22.sales_2022, 0) AS sales_2022,
  COALESCE(y23.sales_2023, 0) AS sales_2023
FROM y23
LEFT JOIN y22
USING (item_number)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Calculate YoY growth % for items that had >0 revenue in 2022.
WITH
  y22 AS (
    SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2022
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2022
    GROUP BY item_number
  ),
  y23 AS (
    SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2023
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2023
    GROUP BY item_number
  )
SELECT
  y23.item_number,
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100 AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM y23
JOIN y22 USING (item_number)
WHERE sales_2022 > 0
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Include descriptive name and filter out negative YoY growth.
WITH
  y22 AS (
    SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2022
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2022
    GROUP BY item_number
  ),
  y23 AS (
    SELECT item_number, SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_2023
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2023
    GROUP BY item_number
  )
SELECT
  y23.item_number,
  ANY_VALUE(item_description) AS item_description, -- descriptive label
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100 AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM y23
JOIN y22 USING (item_number)
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales` s
  ON s.item_number = y23.item_number  -- for description lookup
WHERE sales_2022 > 0
GROUP BY
  y23.item_number,
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER – top 5 items with the highest YoY % growth in total sales revenue from 2022 to 2023.
WITH
  sales_by_year AS (
    SELECT
      item_number,
      item_description,
      EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`)                    AS sales_year,
      SUM(sale_dollars)                            AS year_sales
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) IN (2022, 2023)
    GROUP BY item_number, item_description, sales_year
  ),
  y22 AS (
    SELECT item_number, MAX(item_description) AS item_description, SUM(year_sales) AS sales_2022
    FROM sales_by_year
    WHERE sales_year = 2022
    GROUP BY item_number
  ),
  y23 AS (
    SELECT item_number, SUM(year_sales) AS sales_2023
    FROM sales_by_year
    WHERE sales_year = 2023
    GROUP BY item_number
  )
SELECT
  y23.item_number,
  y22.item_description,
  ROUND(sales_2022, 2)                            AS sales_2022,
  ROUND(sales_2023, 2)                            AS sales_2023,
  ROUND( SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100 , 2) AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM y23
JOIN y22 USING (item_number)
WHERE sales_2022 > 0
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

